You are a senior review consolidator. Multiple independent reviewers have scored the same generated code.
Synthesize their feedback into a single consensus review.

## Original Prompt

Create a TypeScript Node.js project that provides a reusable Azure Blob Storage management utility.

The project needs:

- A **service class** that wraps blob operations: upload (with optional metadata and blob index tags for later querying), download, list blobs in a container, and delete. The upload method should handle large files efficiently using streaming — uploading a multi-gigabyte file should not load the entire thing into memory. The service should also prevent concurrent writers from overwriting each other's changes when updating the same blob by acquiring a lease before writing.

- A **configuration module** that connects to Azure securely using the storage account endpoint (from an environment variable). No connection strings or account keys should be used — the app will run in Azure with managed identity. The configuration should set up a custom retry policy (exponential backoff, configurable max retries and delay) and enable SDK logging at a configurable level for debugging.

- A **main script** that wires everything together and demos each operation: uploads a sample file with some index tags, lists all blobs in the container, downloads the file back and prints its content, acquires a lease and overwrites the blob, then finally deletes it. Print status at each step.

Include a complete `package.json` with the necessary Azure SDK dependencies and a `tsconfig.json`.

## Individual Reviews

### Reviewer 1 (claude-opus-4.6)
```json
{
  "model": "claude-opus-4.6",
  "scores": {
    "criteria": [
      {
        "name": "Code Builds",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "BlobGetPropertiesResponse does not have a 'tags' property (tags require a separate getTags() call). properties.tags in listBlobs() would cause a TypeScript compilation error. Also imports ContainerListBlobFlatSegmentResponse and BlobItem which are unused (though won't error without noUnusedLocals)."
      },
      {
        "name": "Latest Package Versions",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "Specified minimums are significantly outdated: @azure/storage-blob ^12.17.0 (latest 12.31.0), @azure/identity ^4.0.0 (latest 4.13.1), @azure/logger ^1.0.4 (latest 1.3.0). While caret ranges resolve to latest at install time, the minimums signal development against very old SDK versions."
      },
      {
        "name": "Best Practices",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses DefaultAzureCredential, endpoint-based client construction, streaming uploads, async/await throughout, proper retry configuration, and SDK logging."
      },
      {
        "name": "Error Handling",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "No RestError handling anywhere. Generic catch blocks only. No status code inspection for 404 or 409 errors. The uploadWithLease catch block only releases the lease but doesn't differentiate error types."
      },
      {
        "name": "Code Quality",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Clean separation of concerns (config, service, demo). Well-structured classes, clear naming, good use of interfaces. README is comprehensive."
      },
      {
        "name": "Correct @azure/ Scoped Packages",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "All Azure dependencies use @azure/ scoped packages: @azure/storage-blob, @azure/identity, @azure/logger."
      },
      {
        "name": "@azure/identity for Authentication",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Uses DefaultAzureCredential from @azure/identity. No connection strings, account keys, or SAS tokens in code."
      },
      {
        "name": "Client Constructor with Endpoint and Credential",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "BlobServiceClient constructed with endpoint URL and DefaultAzureCredential: new BlobServiceClient(accountUrl, credential, { retryOptions })."
      },
      {
        "name": "Async/Await Pattern",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "All async operations use async/await. Entry point uses main().catch() IIFE pattern."
      },
      {
        "name": "Pagination with for-await-of",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "While listBlobs() correctly uses for-await-of over listBlobsFlat(), it collects ALL results into a BlobInfo[] array via blobs.push() before returning. This is the manual page accumulation anti-pattern the criterion prohibits."
      },
      {
        "name": "LRO Pattern (beginXxx + pollUntilDone)",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Not applicable for blob storage operations (upload, download, list, delete are not LROs). No LRO usage needed for this scenario."
      },
      {
        "name": "RestError Exception Handling",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "RestError is never imported. No statusCode-based error handling. All catch blocks handle generic Error only. No distinction between 404 (not found) and 409 (lease conflict) errors."
      },
      {
        "name": "No Deprecated Packages",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "No deprecated packages present. All dependencies use current @azure/* track."
      },
      {
        "name": "Logging via @azure/logger",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Imports and calls setLogLevel() from @azure/logger. Also configures AzureLogger.log for custom output formatting."
      },
      {
        "name": "package.json with Correct Dependencies",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Valid package.json with all required @azure/* dependencies. Includes tsconfig.json, @types/node, and TypeScript as dev dependencies."
      },
      {
        "name": "Configures custom retry policy via StorageRetryOptions",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Correctly configures StorageRetryOptions with retryPolicyType: EXPONENTIAL, configurable maxRetries and retryDelayInMs from environment variables."
      },
      {
        "name": "Enables SDK logging via @azure/logger setLogLevel()",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Calls setLogLevel() with configurable log level from LOG_LEVEL environment variable."
      },
      {
        "name": "Implements blob lease acquisition using BlobLeaseClient",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "uploadWithLease() correctly uses getBlobLeaseClient(), acquireLease(30), and releaseLease() with proper cleanup in catch block."
      },
      {
        "name": "Uses BlockBlobClient.uploadStream() for streaming upload",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Both uploadStream() and uploadFile() use blockBlobClient.uploadStream() with Readable streams. No uploadData() or full-buffer upload() calls."
      },
      {
        "name": "Sets blob index tags on upload via tags property",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Tags passed through UploadOptions interface to uploadStream() options. Demo sets environment, category, and uploadedBy tags."
      },
      {
        "name": "Downloads blob via readableStreamBody",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "download() method accesses downloadResponse.readableStreamBody and reads it via streamToBuffer() using Node.js Readable stream events."
      },
      {
        "name": "Lists blobs using for-await-of over listBlobsFlat()",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "listBlobs() uses for await (const blob of iterator) over containerClient.listBlobsFlat()."
      },
      {
        "name": "Handles lease conflict errors (409 status code)",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "No 409 status code handling. The uploadWithLease catch block releases the lease but never checks error.statusCode for conflict scenarios."
      },
      {
        "name": "Handles blob not found errors (404 status code)",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "No 404 status code handling in download() or deleteBlob() methods. Both will throw unhandled RestError on missing blobs."
      },
      {
        "name": "NOT using uploadData() or upload() with full buffer",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Correctly uses uploadStream() everywhere. No uploadData() or buffer-based upload() calls."
      },
      {
        "name": "NOT using connection strings or account keys",
        "passed": true,
        "reason": "Authentication uses DefaultAzureCredential with endpoint URL construction. No connection strings or keys anywhere."
      },
      {
        "name": "NOT collecting all listed blobs into array before processing",
        "passed": false,
        "reason": "listBlobs() pushes every blob into a BlobInfo[] array and returns it. The demo then processes this array with forEach(). This defeats the streaming benefit of async iteration."
      }
    ]
  },
  "overall_score": 19,
